Fixed and verified.

**Bug:** `src/sim.ts:43` — `if (foodSurplus >= 0)` grew population on a break-even turn. Since `foodSurplus = foodProduced - foodConsumed`, a settlement merely matching consumption produces `surplus === 0`, which the old condition treated as growth-eligible.

**Fix:** changed `>= 0` to `> 0`, so population only grows on an actual food surplus.

`npm run typecheck` and `npm run test` (4/4) both pass.


